/-!
# Weakly associated points and the base change of a geometric stalk

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S`, let `G` be an
`𝒪_Y`-module and let `x̄` be a geometric point of `X` with image `ȳ`. Write `R = 𝒪_{Y, ȳ}` and
`A = 𝒪_{X, x̄}` for the étale local rings and `φ : R → A` for the canonical homomorphism
between them. Weak association of the maximal ideal of `R` to the geometric stalk `G_{ȳ}` is
compared here with weak association of the maximal ideal of `A` to the base change
`A ⊗_R G_{ȳ}`:

* when `φ` is finite and flat the two conditions are equivalent;
* when `φ` is flat and the maximal ideal of `A` is the radical of the ideal generated by the
  maximal ideal of `R` — that is, when the fibre of `f` at `x̄` has a zero-dimensional local
  ring — the first implies the second.

## Main results

* `isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_maximalIdeal_tensorProduct_iff_of_finite_flat`: for a finite flat
  local homomorphism of local rings, weak association of the maximal ideal is equivalent to
  weak association of the maximal ideal of the target to the base change.
* `isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_maximalIdeal_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_radical_eq`: for a flat local
  homomorphism whose extension of the maximal ideal has the maximal ideal as its radical, weak
  association of the maximal ideal passes to the base change.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_geometricModuleStalk_modulePullback_iff`:
  **Stacks 0CUT** at the étale local ring, for a finite flat morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_geometricModuleStalk_baseChange_iff`: the
  same equivalence at a free module universe, stated for the base change that the geometric
  stalk of `f^*G` is identified with.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_geometricModuleStalk_baseChange`: the
  stalkwise content of Stacks 0CUA, for a morphism flat at the point whose fibre there has a
  zero-dimensional local ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPoint_modulePullback`: **Stacks 0CUA** itself.

## Implementation notes

Weak association of a point of an algebraic space,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsWeaklyAssociatedPoint`, is weak association of the maximal ideal of
the étale local ring to the geometric stalk of Stacks 05VQ, so the statements below are the
stalkwise content of the two source lemmas. They are stated for the base change
`A ⊗_R G_{ȳ}`; the identification of that base change with the geometric stalk of the pullback
`f^*G` is the base-change clause of Stacks 05VQ,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricModuleStalkPullbackIso`, which carries no hypotheses, and it
is what turns the stalkwise form of Stacks 0CUA into the tag itself. The remaining step is that
weak association does not depend on the geometric point chosen above a point of `|X|`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPoint_iff_isWeaklyAssociatedPrime`. Along an étale
morphism the two étale local rings coincide and the corresponding statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPoint_modulePullback_iff`.

The zero-dimensionality of the local ring of the fibre is expressed as the equality of the
maximal ideal of `A` with the radical of the ideal `𝔪_R A`: the local ring of the fibre at `x̄`
is `A / 𝔪_R A`, whose maximal ideal is `𝔪_A / 𝔪_R A`, and that quotient has dimension zero
exactly when every element of `𝔪_A` has a power in `𝔪_R A`.

Both hypotheses of Stacks 0CUT are read on the morphism of algebraic spaces. Flatness passes to
the canonical homomorphism of étale local rings by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_etaleLocalRingMap`, and finiteness by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.finite_etaleLocalRingMap`: the source argues that the strict
henselization of a finite algebra splits as a finite product of strictly henselian local rings,
so the étale local ring upstairs is a factor of a finite `𝒪_{Y, ȳ}`-algebra; the route taken
here instead reads both étale local rings off an affine chart square over `f` whose chart
morphism is a finite morphism of affine schemes, where the comparison of Stacks 04KF makes the
homomorphism the map of strict henselizations along a finite ring map, finite by Stacks 05WR.
The ring-level form at a general finite flat local homomorphism,
`isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_maximalIdeal_tensorProduct_iff_of_finite_flat`, and its geometric
restatement `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isWeaklyAssociatedPrime_geometricModuleStalk_baseChange_iff`
keep finiteness on the homomorphism, since that is all their proofs use.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CUT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CUT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CUA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CUA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CTX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CTX)
